Update the Alva game’s Home screen and credits presentation. Work within the existing architecture and visual language. This is a plain HTML/CSS/vanilla-JavaScript browser fighting game with no framework and no build step. Do not modify combat, physics, fighter sprite rendering, stage rendering, input systems, or unrelated menu screens.

Files/context to inspect first

The main relevant files are:

* js/screens/home-screen.js — constructs the Home screen.
* styles.css — Home layout begins around the .screen--home / .home-* rules.
* js/ui/help-content.js — current Help and Credits content.
* js/screens/help-credits-screen.js — existing Help & Credits screen.
* js/core/app.js — screen registration.
* ALVA_SPEC.md and README.md — update documentation where needed so it does not contradict the finished UI.

Preserve Alva’s existing near-black/charcoal/off-white/green design system and its existing geometric SVG wordmark.

1. Reposition the large ALVA wordmark

On the Home screen, move the large ALVA wordmark farther to the left.

The visible left edge of the first “A” glyph should line up with the exact horizontal starting position of the supporting text below it.

The supporting text currently starts with “Fast…”, so the intended visual instruction is: put ALVA where the word “Fast” currently starts.

Do this as a Home-specific layout adjustment. Do not modify the global logo.js wordmark geometry in a way that changes the logo everywhere else.

If the SVG element is technically aligned but its visible glyph still appears inset, compensate in the Home-only CSS with positioning/translation so the visible first stroke of the A aligns with the text.

2. Change the Home tagline

Replace:

Fast, responsive fighting in your browser.

with exactly:

Fan project. Big heart.

Keep the same general typography hierarchy and muted supporting-text treatment unless spacing needs adjustment for the redesigned layout.

3. Remove the “2D sprite fighting game” Home text

Completely remove the visible Home eyebrow:

2D sprite fighting game

Do not merely hide it with opacity. Remove the element from the Home DOM and remove/rework any spacing that existed specifically for .home-eyebrow.

This request concerns the visible Home UI; do not break useful technical metadata solely because similar descriptive wording exists elsewhere.

