Remove the small decorative ALVA logo currently shown in the Home header at the top left.

The large central ALVA wordmark remains.

Remove unused markup/CSS/imports associated specifically with the small Home header logo where appropriate.

5. Remove the top-right Build label

Remove the Home-screen text such as:

Build 0.1.0

There should be no build/version label in the upper-right corner of Home.

After removing both the small ALVA mark and Build label, do not leave an empty header taking up unnecessary vertical space. Reclaim that space for the main Home composition.

Do not remove CONFIG.version globally if it is useful elsewhere.

6. Disable Help & Credits from Home for now

Keep the visible Help & Credits button on the Home menu, but disable it for now.

Requirements:

* Use a genuinely disabled button state.
* It must not navigate to the Help & Credits screen.
* It must not receive keyboard/gamepad menu focus.
* It must not react to click/touch.
* Give it a restrained disabled appearance consistent with Alva’s existing charcoal/gray hierarchy.
* Keep its text readable.
* Play remains the default focused Home action.

Do not delete the underlying Help/credits infrastructure because Help is still used from the battle pause menu and may be re-enabled later.

7. Completely remove the decorative road

Delete the Home road visual.

Remove:

* the angled road surface,
* lane markings,
* lane animation,
* road-specific masking,
* road scrolling keyframes,
* road-specific responsive positioning,
* any other CSS or DOM that only exists to render the road.

There should be no visual trace of a roadway.

8. Replace the road area with an infinite vertical credits section

Use the area that was previously occupied by the road as a dedicated credits panel on the right side of Home.

Visual design

The new credits region should:

* occupy approximately the same right-side visual zone that the road used,
* have a gray/charcoal background that is clearly distinct from the near-black menu background,
* contain upright, readable credit text,
* use Alva’s existing typography,
* remain restrained and clean rather than looking like an arcade marquee.

Place a crisp green separator line along the left boundary of the credits region, visually separating the left-side Home menu from the right-side credits panel.

The separator should use the existing Alva green accent. A roughly 3px divider is appropriate and should visually replace the role the old road’s green slash played.

Do not introduce new accent colors.

9. Infinite credits scrolling behavior

The credits inside the right panel should automatically move vertically upward at a slow, readable, constant speed.

Behavior:

1. Credits enter/move upward through the visible panel.
2. The entire credit sequence continues until all text has completely passed out of view.
3. Once the complete sequence has passed, restart it from the beginning.
4. Continue indefinitely.

A seamless duplicated-track loop is acceptable and preferable if it avoids a visible hitch, but a clean reset after the final text has fully passed is also acceptable.

Do not create timers that accumulate or duplicate themselves every time Home is entered.

Accessibility

For prefers-reduced-motion: reduce:

* disable the automatic movement,
* present the credits in a readable static state instead.

If duplicated DOM is used to create the infinite animation, expose only one copy to assistive technology and mark animation-only duplicates aria-hidden="true".

