14. Responsive behavior

Preserve the current requirement that Home fits the viewport without page scrolling and respects safe-area insets.

Test at minimum:

* normal desktop landscape,
* wide desktop,
* narrow desktop,
* short landscape heights,
* touch/mobile landscape,
* very short landscape layouts.

The Home menu must remain legible and usable even when the viewport height is constrained.

The credits panel should not overlap the menu or make the Play button inaccessible.

If the viewport becomes too narrow for a comfortable side-by-side presentation, intelligently reduce the credits-panel footprint while preserving the green separator and keeping the main ALVA/menu content dominant. Do not bring the road back.

